From 7b14288e6eb26380c7fb112cb65b3029cc88635a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: molintc <marek.olczak@intel.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 12:31:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add XPU device recognition to the TBE frontend

Recognize XPU in the Python TBE frontend without adding backend policy or
changing the existing CPU, CUDA, and MTIA paths:

- append XPU to ComputeDevice so existing enum values remain stable;
- allow DEVICE placement and select XPU only when it is available after
  CUDA and MTIA;
- avoid CUDA device queries when Split TBE selects XPU, and let Dense TBE
  receive an explicit device;
- select XPU in shared TBE utility allocation helpers;
- add focused CPU-only tests for recognition, priority, and device-query
  behavior.

This patch only enables frontend device recognition. It does not add
kernels, change operator schemas, impose plugin capability restrictions,
or alter inference, cache, or bounds-check behavior.
